1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,267
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,433
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:44,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,367
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,833
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:49,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,267
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,167
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:55,500
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,200
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,567
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:09,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,867
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:13,233
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,333
<i> I thought Papa trusted me now.</i>

21
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:24,033
<i> A person gets sharper</i>

22
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:26,067
<i>when they have someone
to compete with.</i>

23
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:27,400
<i> Listen up, everyone!</i>

24
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,533
<i>If anyone gets in your way,
take them out.</i>

25
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:30,400
<i>- You're the boss.
- Just sign here.</i>

26
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,900
<i>This means you are choosing
Rudy Magtibay</i>

27
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:37,367
<i>to be
your community's representative.</i>

28
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:39,400
<i>You know, when I was a kid,
I loved doing the laundry</i>

29
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,000
<i>because I used to play
with the bubbles.</i>

30
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:42,000
<i> Like this.</i>

31
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:46,767
<i>- See, you've got bubbles now.
- You've got bubbles, too!</i>

32
00:01:46,767 --> 00:01:48,433
<i> They suit each other.</i>

33
00:01:48,433 --> 00:01:50,367
I hope they do end up together.

34
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:54,433
Love, I'll take care of this.
I'll rinse the clothes.

35
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:56,367
It'd be better
if you hang the clothes.

36
00:01:57,333 --> 00:01:58,333
Alright.

37
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,300
Wait a minute, before we...

38
00:02:01,367 --> 00:02:04,567
...throw the soapy water away,
can we pour it on the floor,

39
00:02:04,567 --> 00:02:07,800
and then brush it,
so we get to clean the floor?

40
00:02:08,933 --> 00:02:11,600
[DIDAY] That's right, Gloria.
That's a great idea.

41
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,867
I think we should also
tell everyone else

42
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,967
to clean their surroundings

43
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:20,333
to prevent the cause of dengue
and the cause of leptospirosis.

44
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:24,433
My gossipy neighbors!

45
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,800
Did you hear what Gloria said?

46
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:32,033
We'll pour
our laundry water here,

47
00:02:32,033 --> 00:02:33,700
so we can brush the floor clean,

48
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,467
and so your mouths can
become clean, too.

49
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:39,067
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

50
00:02:39,067 --> 00:02:41,533
- Where's our broom?
- It's over there, I'll get it.

51
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:48,433
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:10,567
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:03:10,567 --> 00:03:13,667
- [MAN] Lower!
- Go on, lower!

54
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:15,133
Dance with Gabo!

55
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:19,800
[LAUGHTER]

56
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:30,033
[OBJECTS RUSTLING]

57
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:32,500
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,500
That damn woman.

59
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:39,400
So you chose to fool me, huh?

60
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,000
Let's see, Miss Pretty.

61
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,100
When we meet later...

62
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:49,933
You won't be
Miss Pretty anymore.

63
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:55,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

64
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:59,567
Hey! What is this nonsense?

65
00:03:59,567 --> 00:04:02,433
You're making a mess again.

66
00:04:08,567 --> 00:04:11,033
You know what,
Gloria's so smart!

67
00:04:11,033 --> 00:04:12,533
And she's even kind!

68
00:04:12,533 --> 00:04:15,967
She's teaching us
to make Paradise a better place.

69
00:04:15,967 --> 00:04:19,467
- You're just too much.
- [ELTON] She's right, Betchay.

70
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,733
Gloria's such a godsend
to all of us.

71
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:25,667
We'll clean this place
for us and for the kids!

72
00:04:25,667 --> 00:04:28,233
It's time we make
those mosquitoes disappear.

73
00:04:28,267 --> 00:04:30,867
And those rats
that keep running around, too!

74
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:32,533
We'll make our community better!

75
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:35,100
[NEIGHBORS] That's right!

76
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:38,000
[BETCHAY]
You believe that woman?

77
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,233
She's just fooling you!

78
00:04:40,233 --> 00:04:41,833
What does she even know?

79
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:44,600
All of a sudden, she'll borrow
money from all of you,

80
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:48,767
but she'll run away
and won't pay!

81
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:50,500
She's a criminal, after all!

82
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,000
- [MAMENG] Hey!
- Oh my god!

83
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,600
Can't you see the good
in people anymore?

84
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,167
What, you think everyone's evil?

85
00:04:56,167 --> 00:04:59,033
[RUDY] Betchay. Stop speaking
badly about others!

86
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:02,067
If you don't believe,
then do whatever you want!

87
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,600
I've been doing as I please
for a long time!

88
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,100
I won't get rich from this,
after all.

89
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,200
[DIDAY] Come on,
don't mind Betchay!

90
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:12,733
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

91
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:15,200
[DIDAY]
Let's continue, come on!

92
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:19,800
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

93
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:24,200
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,167
You okay?

95
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:29,500
- I'm sorry.
- Don't mind it.

96
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:35,233
[BETCHAY] That Gloria
is such a show-off.

97
00:05:35,267 --> 00:05:38,567
Who does she think she is?
She's just new here.

98
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:41,133
She wants everyone
to follow her.

99
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:45,167
Hey! I don't care
if you came from prison.

100
00:05:45,167 --> 00:05:47,133
You can't make me obey you!

101
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,967
But...

102
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:52,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:53,800
Her idea's nice.

104
00:05:55,667 --> 00:05:57,900
I will use that in the bar.

105
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:02,200
So we become more profitable...

106
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:05,567
I'll clean the bar.

107
00:06:06,133 --> 00:06:07,633
[CHUCKLES]

108
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,233
You better be ready for me.

109
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:14,000
[GABO] Love, I'm sorry
you got tired.

110
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,000
We washed so many clothes.

111
00:06:16,767 --> 00:06:19,567
We even washed Papa's clothes.

112
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,600
I'm the one embarrassed

113
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,633
because I don't know
how to do laundry.

114
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:24,767
Not really.

115
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:27,200
You just forgot about that.
But I'm sure,

116
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,267
you'll soon remember
how to do laundry.

117
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Gabo.

118
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,567
Can I ask you for something?

119
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,667
What is it, love?

120
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,300
I've been missing
Miss Berta's barbecue.

121
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:45,633
Sure!

122
00:06:45,633 --> 00:06:48,033
We can even have that
for dinner tonight.

123
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:50,067
- Really?
- Yes. Go on.

124
00:06:50,067 --> 00:06:51,833
Pick what you want. I'll pay.

125
00:06:52,733 --> 00:06:53,867
Alright, thank you.

126
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:58,233
[DIDAY] Want to get a manicure
and a pedicure?

127
00:06:58,233 --> 00:06:59,900
Maybe next time.

128
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:03,000
[DIDAY] Alright. Tell me, okay?
It's on me.

129
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,300
Okay, thank you.

130
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,867
[NEIGHBOR] Miss Diday,
don't hurt my nails.

131
00:07:06,867 --> 00:07:09,400
[DIDAY] I'll really hurt you
if you're too dramatic!

132
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:13,633
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:15,633
Seems like
you really like that, Gloria.

134
00:07:15,667 --> 00:07:18,867
Yes, this is the best barbecue
I have ever tasted.

135
00:07:18,867 --> 00:07:20,900
There are a lot of food stalls
here in Tondo.

136
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:23,200
- You know about Ugbo?
- Ugbo? No.

137
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,667
That's one
of the top food spots here.

138
00:07:25,667 --> 00:07:28,767
You can invite Gabo to go
on a date there. It'll be fun!

139
00:07:28,767 --> 00:07:31,367
- I'll tell Gabo.
- [ESTONG] You'll enjoy it.

140
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:32,867
[BERTA] I'll just cook it.

141
00:07:32,867 --> 00:07:34,833
- I'll call you when it's done.
- Alright, thank you.

142
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:36,233
[TEK] Gloria!

143
00:07:36,333 --> 00:07:39,167
You're good at laundry!
And you're so hardworking!

144
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,167
Gabo is so lucky to have you!

145
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:45,200
No. I'm the one lucky
with my husband.

146
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,900
Well, did you hear that?

147
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,367
She's the lucky one
for being with me!

148
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:53,433
[KULAS] You're right, Gabo!
You're lucky to have Gloria.

149
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:56,200
She's not just beautiful,
but also hardworking.

150
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,433
Unlike my wife.

151
00:07:58,433 --> 00:08:01,133
[ESTONG] Hey, Pa!
Mama might hear you.

152
00:08:01,133 --> 00:08:04,067
She'll beat you up again,
but you like that, don't you?

153
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:06,967
Why? It's true
that your mom seduced me!

154
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:10,400
Mister Kulas. I think you miss
Miss Diday's punches.

155
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:13,033
- Not really, Gabo.
- [GABO CHUCKLES]

156
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:14,467
That's everything.

157
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:17,667
- Hey, Tek, the water's open.
- Okay, Gabo. I'll handle it.

158
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:23,067
You know, Miss Berta is famous
here for her barbecue.

159
00:08:24,833 --> 00:08:27,767
She's the star every time
there's booze involved!

160
00:08:28,433 --> 00:08:30,033
- [SAM CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- [GABO GRUNTS]

161
00:08:31,433 --> 00:08:32,900
- [LAUNDRY BASKET THUDS]
- [GABO GRUNTS]

162
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:36,000
It's really fun here
in your community.

163
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:40,133
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:43,933
You know, love,
even though we're poor...

165
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,333
even though some have not
gone to school

166
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:47,467
or have graduated...

167
00:08:48,167 --> 00:08:51,900
...they all still love
and respect each other.

168
00:08:52,433 --> 00:08:56,000
So, even though we live
a very simple life,

169
00:08:56,033 --> 00:08:57,167
we're still very happy.

170
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:02,167
Yeah. I think it's really fun
to live here.

171
00:09:03,367 --> 00:09:05,400
But it's also unfortunate.

172
00:09:07,867 --> 00:09:08,900
How come?

173
00:09:12,767 --> 00:09:14,533
U-Uhh...

174
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:17,300
I just read something. That...

175
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:21,833
...Ginintuang Lupa is owned
by the Jacintos?

176
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:23,267
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

177
00:09:23,267 --> 00:09:24,933
[GABO SCOFFS]

178
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,867
You know, love,
you shouldn't believe that.

179
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,233
That's not true.

180
00:09:29,233 --> 00:09:30,800
The land here...

181
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:34,533
We invested our blood, sweat,
and tears for it.

182
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:37,167
No one can take this land
from us.

183
00:09:37,167 --> 00:09:38,833
We'll fight until death
for this.

184
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:42,533
Hey, Betchay.

185
00:09:42,533 --> 00:09:44,167
- Huh?
- The one who paid for damages,

186
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:45,800
has she talked to Rudy?

187
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:49,133
- What damages?
- From the previous demolition.

188
00:09:49,133 --> 00:09:51,200
It's 5000 pesos per family!

189
00:09:52,867 --> 00:09:56,067
That-- That tall beautiful
fair-skinned woman

190
00:09:56,067 --> 00:09:58,200
who was with a lawyer?

191
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:03,300
They asked who our leader was.
We said it's Rudy.

192
00:10:03,333 --> 00:10:05,267
Hasn't anyone talked
to you yet?

193
00:10:05,267 --> 00:10:08,000
We turned down that offer.

194
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,267
That damn woman.
She said it was 300,000 pesos.

195
00:10:12,267 --> 00:10:13,833
- What a fraud.
- What's that, Betchay?

196
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:17,033
Oh, nothing. Nothing.
We rejected that offer.

197
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:18,400
Ohh, okay.

198
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:23,400
She was really gonna fool me.

199
00:10:29,267 --> 00:10:31,400
I just had a thought.

200
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:34,467
If those people were making
Papa Rudy sign...

201
00:10:35,267 --> 00:10:38,100
They might've been successful
in having others sign it.

202
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:41,300
I don't think so.

203
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:44,033
Even though the residents here
are like that...

204
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,933
They're still intelligent.

205
00:10:47,467 --> 00:10:49,267
They can't just make them sign.

206
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:54,433
I know,
but if they fooled Mama Betchay,

207
00:10:54,433 --> 00:10:58,033
maybe, just maybe,
someone else signed.

208
00:10:58,567 --> 00:11:01,100
Maybe we can talk to them
and ask?

209
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:08,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:13,167
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:11:13,167 --> 00:11:14,700
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [DOOR SLAMS SHUT]

212
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:21,967
[BAG THUDS]

213
00:11:23,133 --> 00:11:25,433
[BILL SPIKE THUDS, CLATTERS]

214
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

215
00:11:30,933 --> 00:11:32,233
This is all we earned
last night?

216
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,167
Do you see anything else
listed there?

217
00:11:34,167 --> 00:11:37,067
Nothing! Zero last night!
Zero, Betchay!

218
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:38,067
Hey.

219
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:41,800
What the hell happened?

220
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:44,467
Betchay, we have no customers!
No one comes in!

221
00:11:44,467 --> 00:11:46,467
Whenever I run things here,

222
00:11:46,467 --> 00:11:48,500
- BeerGin makes money!
- [PRISCILLA] Betchay...

223
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,167
Customers don't come
back anymore

224
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,167
because you just trick them!

225
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:53,467
Trick them?

226
00:11:53,467 --> 00:11:55,833
Remember those pictures
you wanted posted outside?

227
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:57,833
That's called promo!

228
00:11:57,833 --> 00:12:01,000
- Promo?
- Marketing strategy!

229
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,833
Well, they didn't like it.
They felt scammed.

230
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:07,500
Hey, I had to find a way

231
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,500
for BeerGin to earn!

232
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,500
Because if I relied on you,

233
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,933
we'd have nothing!

234
00:12:12,933 --> 00:12:14,867
Just look at yourselves!

235
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,400
Hey, you've crossed
the line now!

236
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,367
[BETCHAY] No, seriously!
Look at yourselves!

237
00:12:19,367 --> 00:12:21,367
Be honest.

238
00:12:21,367 --> 00:12:23,133
You look completely worn out.

239
00:12:23,133 --> 00:12:24,233
Come on, Betchay!

240
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:27,533
You act like you're not
the same age as us!

241
00:12:27,533 --> 00:12:30,500
- Excuse me!
- You've got some nerve!

242
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,300
I still look thirty!

243
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:34,500
[ROSANNA] What?
You're so full of yourself!

244
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,367
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

245
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:37,967
- [OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ENGINES HUMMING]

246
00:12:37,967 --> 00:12:39,033
[CAR DOORS OPEN]

247
00:12:39,033 --> 00:12:40,533
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

248
00:12:40,533 --> 00:12:41,533
[CAR DOORS SLAM SHUT]

249
00:12:41,533 --> 00:12:46,200
[HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

250
00:12:50,567 --> 00:12:54,533
Papa said there aren't
many guards back here.

251
00:12:54,533 --> 00:12:56,467
That's where we come in, boss.

252
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,567
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

253
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:03,533
Who's that?

254
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:04,500
Hang on!

255
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:06,200
He works for me.

256
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,400
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE TURNS OFF]

257
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,200
He's my backup plan, boss.

258
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:13,333
What do you mean?

259
00:13:13,767 --> 00:13:15,033
You'll find out soon enough.

260
00:13:15,033 --> 00:13:17,833
He's gonna save our skins later.

261
00:13:17,833 --> 00:13:24,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:13:24,567 --> 00:13:25,867
Where's the jacket?

263
00:13:26,567 --> 00:13:27,767
Galo.

264
00:13:34,233 --> 00:13:35,333
[GATE HANDLE CLANKING]

265
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,200
[COP 1 GRUNTS]

266
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,267
[GATE RATTLES]

267
00:13:39,267 --> 00:13:40,567
- [HEAVY THUD]
- [COP 2 WHIMPERS]

268
00:13:40,567 --> 00:13:47,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:13:47,267 --> 00:13:48,600
Once bullets start flying,

270
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,067
get the motorcycle inside fast.

271
00:13:50,067 --> 00:13:51,433
- Okay, boss.
- Let's meet inside.

272
00:13:51,433 --> 00:13:55,567
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

273
00:13:58,433 --> 00:13:59,433
Everyone!

274
00:14:00,333 --> 00:14:01,500
Come closer.

275
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,933
Listen up.

276
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:04,400
I have something to tell you.

277
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,267
- [GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

278
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:08,900
This morning,

279
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,533
two people came
into our house.

280
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,400
They wanted Papa
to sign a document.

281
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,900
They pretended to be
from an NGO,

282
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:22,633
saying it was supposed to help
those hit by the demolition.

283
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:24,400
[OVERLAPPING MURMURS]

284
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,967
But then Gloria looked
through the papers...

285
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:32,100
And she saw that
they needed our signatures...

286
00:14:32,867 --> 00:14:36,933
...so that the Jacintos
can take our land!

287
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:43,433
[NEIGHBORS CLAMORING]

288
00:14:43,433 --> 00:14:49,133
I'm here to tell you all
not to sign any document!

289
00:14:49,133 --> 00:14:52,100
Make sure you know
the people approaching you.

290
00:14:52,867 --> 00:14:58,167
They'll come here to woo you,
and to convince you

291
00:14:58,167 --> 00:15:02,200
to sign a document
we don't know the contents of!

292
00:15:02,233 --> 00:15:04,367
[ESTONG]
Gabo, earlier, just outside,

293
00:15:04,367 --> 00:15:06,067
I saw people asking
for signatures.

294
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:07,633
[NEIGHBOR 1]
That's the 5000 pesos!

295
00:15:07,633 --> 00:15:10,967
They said it was for those
affected by the demolition!

296
00:15:10,967 --> 00:15:12,500
They said it's for that!

297
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:16,500
[NEIGHBOR 2]
But I signed it too, Gabo.

298
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,000
But it was in English,
so I couldn't understand it.

299
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,367
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

300
00:15:20,367 --> 00:15:21,467
You signed it?!

301
00:15:24,367 --> 00:15:26,000
[NEIGHBOR 3]
Gabo, they said

302
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:30,300
that they'll make Mister Rudy
our community's representative.

303
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:33,500
Did they explain
what document you were signing?

304
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:36,333
They said it was
for special power?

305
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:40,500
That must be the special power
of an attorney.

306
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,167
[NEIGHBOR 2]
Yes, that's it, Gloria!

307
00:15:42,167 --> 00:15:46,267
[NEIGHBOR 3] They said we'll
follow Mister Rudy's decisions,

308
00:15:46,267 --> 00:15:47,567
so we signed it.

309
00:15:47,567 --> 00:15:51,167
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

310
00:15:51,167 --> 00:15:52,500
- I told you not to sign!
- Wait!

311
00:15:53,333 --> 00:15:55,533
So if I signed that document...

312
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,067
We're all going
to get kicked out of here!

313
00:15:59,067 --> 00:16:00,533
What do you mean, Rudy?

314
00:16:01,933 --> 00:16:04,333
Mister Kulas, that just means

315
00:16:04,333 --> 00:16:07,700
that once Papa Rudy signs it,
he is agreeing...

316
00:16:08,433 --> 00:16:10,267
...to have all of you evicted
from Ginintuang Lupa

317
00:16:10,267 --> 00:16:11,367
in exchange for money.

318
00:16:11,367 --> 00:16:16,433
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

319
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:19,300
[DIDAY]
Those people are so shameless!

320
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:22,267
When they come back here,
I'll push them in the gutter.

321
00:16:22,267 --> 00:16:24,733
[NEIGHBOR 3] What now, Gloria?
We've signed it!

322
00:16:25,633 --> 00:16:27,100
Let's all calm down.

323
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:30,100
As long as Papa Rudy
does not sign the document,

324
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,567
nothing bad will happen.

325
00:16:31,567 --> 00:16:33,600
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

326
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,500
Neighbors.

327
00:16:35,567 --> 00:16:40,433
I will never sell our community,
so don't worry!

328
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:41,433
-That's right.
-That's right.

329
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:46,233
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

330
00:16:46,233 --> 00:16:48,300
- Thank you so much!
- Thank you!

331
00:16:50,133 --> 00:16:51,500
Let's do it this way.

332
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:55,067
When they come back,
and ask you to sign something...

333
00:16:55,667 --> 00:16:57,267
Do not sign it.

334
00:16:58,133 --> 00:17:01,633
Bring it to our house,
so Gloria can read what it is.

335
00:17:01,633 --> 00:17:04,233
- Do you understand?
- [NEIGHBORS] Yes!

336
00:17:04,233 --> 00:17:07,567
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

337
00:17:07,567 --> 00:17:11,233
When you see them again here,
drive them away!

338
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:13,233
They cannot kick us out of here!

339
00:17:13,233 --> 00:17:16,267
We drove away the Jacintos!
We can drive them away too!

340
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:17,367
[NEIGHBORS] That's right!

341
00:17:17,367 --> 00:17:19,833
[NEIGHBORS CLAMORING]

342
00:17:19,833 --> 00:17:22,300
[SAM]  Dad bought all
of their lands here.

343
00:17:23,133 --> 00:17:25,133
<i>So what will happen
to the people living here?</i>

344
00:17:26,367 --> 00:17:27,600
<i> Where will they go?</i>

345
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:32,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

346
00:17:33,167 --> 00:17:35,033
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:17:35,033 --> 00:17:38,967
[ROLL-UP DOOR RATTLING]

348
00:17:49,833 --> 00:17:56,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:00,133
[COP 1 GRUNTS]

350
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:01,833
- [KICK, BLOW LAND]
- [GROANING]

351
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:02,800
[BODY THUDS]

352
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:04,167
[LUCAS] Out of my way!

353
00:18:13,033 --> 00:18:14,033
[COP 2 GRUNTS]

354
00:18:14,033 --> 00:18:15,733
- [LOUD THWACKS]
- [BODY THUDS]

355
00:18:15,733 --> 00:18:21,333
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:22,600
Boss.

357
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,367
We should strike now.

358
00:18:29,367 --> 00:18:30,733
We outnumber them.

359
00:18:31,333 --> 00:18:33,867
[DJANGO] Boss, don't rush it.

360
00:18:34,367 --> 00:18:35,800
Let's wait a little longer.

361
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,833
What are we waiting for?

362
00:18:37,833 --> 00:18:39,400
We're just wasting time.

363
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,733
[SNICKERS]

364
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:42,833
Right now,
there aren't many of them.

365
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:45,833
But I'm sure they've got
backup coming.

366
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,067
See those guards?

367
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,667
We'll wait until
they switch shifts,

368
00:18:49,667 --> 00:18:51,100
then we strike.

369
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:52,833
Once their defenses drop,

370
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:55,367
that's when we grab the gold.
Sounds good?

371
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,600
[CHUCKLES]

372
00:18:57,367 --> 00:18:58,733
Dudo, Galo.

373
00:18:59,067 --> 00:19:00,100
See if it's open.

374
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:01,767
Faster!

375
00:19:03,367 --> 00:19:05,900
[ROLL-UP DOOR RATTLING]

376
00:19:06,767 --> 00:19:07,733
Positive, boss.

377
00:19:09,067 --> 00:19:10,067
Boss.

378
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:13,267
I'll head in first.

379
00:19:13,267 --> 00:19:14,767
I'll scope it out

380
00:19:14,767 --> 00:19:16,133
and see where
they stashed the gold.

381
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:18,633
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

382
00:19:18,633 --> 00:19:19,867
I call the shots, remember?

383
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:21,400
Right.

384
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,400
Sorry.

385
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,600
Wait right here, sir.

386
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,633
No.

387
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:27,900
We're going with you.

388
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:29,733
We don't trust you.

389
00:19:30,133 --> 00:19:32,633
Okay. You're the boss.

390
00:19:33,133 --> 00:19:35,667
- Lao, come with me.
- [CHUCKLES]

391
00:19:35,667 --> 00:19:37,333
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

392
00:19:37,333 --> 00:19:38,733
[DJANGO] Boys, stay here.

393
00:19:38,733 --> 00:19:40,733
Wait for my signal
before going in.

394
00:19:40,733 --> 00:19:41,700
Yes, boss.

395
00:19:45,333 --> 00:19:46,867
Boss, there's CCTV.

396
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,400
[DJANGO] Shut it down!

397
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:49,867
Hurry!

398
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:53,767
- [CABLE SNAPS]
- [DIGITAL WHIRRING]

399
00:19:53,767 --> 00:19:55,767
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

400
00:19:55,767 --> 00:19:56,733
Get in!

401
00:20:10,033 --> 00:20:17,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:20:26,333 --> 00:20:27,300
[DOOR OPENS]

404
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

405
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,133
We're being watched!

406
00:20:31,133 --> 00:20:32,067
End it!

407
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,433
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

408
00:20:40,467 --> 00:20:44,300
[DIGITAL WHIRRING, CRACKLING]

409
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:51,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

410
00:20:54,067 --> 00:20:55,167
[DIGITAL WHIRRING,
CRACKLING CONTINUES]

411
00:20:56,233 --> 00:20:57,233
[DOOR OPENS]

412
00:20:57,233 --> 00:20:58,733
- [LOUD THWACKS]
- [GROANING]

413
00:20:58,733 --> 00:20:59,700
[BODY THUDS]

414
00:21:01,467 --> 00:21:02,700
Upstairs!

415
00:21:06,033 --> 00:21:13,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

416
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:21,000
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

417
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,967
[DOOR OPENS]

418
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,233
[PAPERS RUSTLE]

419
00:21:35,867 --> 00:21:39,067
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

420
00:21:39,067 --> 00:21:40,367
- [KICK LANDS]
- [DOOR RATTLES]

421
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,433
Drop your gun.

422
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:46,967
[LOUD THWACKS]

423
00:21:46,967 --> 00:21:47,933
[BODY THUDS]

424
00:21:49,567 --> 00:21:50,533
[CRATE THUDDING]

425
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,833
[LID OPENS]

426
00:21:54,967 --> 00:21:56,133
The gold is here.

427
00:21:56,133 --> 00:21:57,533
[POLICE SIREN BLARES]

428
00:21:57,533 --> 00:22:01,600
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

429
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,600
The cops just rolled in!

430
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:03,800
[DJANGO] Move faster!

431
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,533
[CRATE RATTLING, THUDS]

432
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:12,400
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

433
00:22:12,867 --> 00:22:14,400
Team, fall in!

434
00:22:16,267 --> 00:22:19,133
Let's do a roll call
before the duty shift!

435
00:22:19,133 --> 00:22:20,100
[IN UNISON] Yes, sir!

436
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:27,600
- I've got the jewelry!
- Hurry up!

437
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:29,967
Quickly!

438
00:22:29,967 --> 00:22:34,467
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

439
00:22:34,467 --> 00:22:36,133
- Buenaventura!
- Present!

440
00:22:36,133 --> 00:22:37,933
- Candido!
- Yes, sir!

441
00:22:43,167 --> 00:22:44,133
[GRUNTS]

442
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:46,600
- Dela Cruz!
- Yes, sir!

443
00:22:48,333 --> 00:22:51,967
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,967
Move it!

445
00:23:07,667 --> 00:23:09,000
[GUN CLATTERS]

446
00:23:10,133 --> 00:23:17,067
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

447
00:23:28,167 --> 00:23:28,967
[LUCAS] Pick up the pace!

448
00:23:28,967 --> 00:23:31,167
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

449
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:32,100
Hurry!

450
00:23:33,233 --> 00:23:34,200
Move it!

451
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,867
- Let's go!
- Double time!

452
00:23:41,067 --> 00:23:42,000
[GRUNTS]

453
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:44,000
[DJANGO] Come on!

454
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:48,133
Trinidad!

455
00:23:48,133 --> 00:23:52,300
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:53,200
[GROANS]

457
00:23:53,833 --> 00:23:56,833
[PHONE RINGING]

458
00:23:57,733 --> 00:23:59,700
- Hello?
<i> - Sir, we've got intruders!</i>

459
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:00,700
What?!

460
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:02,667
- [GOON GRUNTING]
- [CRATE THUDS]

461
00:24:06,533 --> 00:24:07,700
- This way!
- Hang on...

462
00:24:08,333 --> 00:24:09,567
Where's the other crate?

463
00:24:09,567 --> 00:24:11,033
Did you get it?

464
00:24:11,033 --> 00:24:12,567
Damn you, Django.

465
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,300
He might have double-crossed us.

466
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,433
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

467
00:24:17,433 --> 00:24:18,600
Rivera!

468
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:20,333
Sir, they must still be inside.

469
00:24:22,700 --> 00:24:23,667
Sir, we've got company!

470
00:24:23,667 --> 00:24:24,733
- Get them!
- Follow me!

471
00:24:24,733 --> 00:24:25,933
Come on!

472
00:24:25,933 --> 00:24:26,900
Hey!

473
00:24:27,533 --> 00:24:28,533
[GUNSHOTS]

474
00:24:28,567 --> 00:24:29,500
My gun!

475
00:24:30,567 --> 00:24:31,567
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

476
00:24:31,567 --> 00:24:32,567
[GROANS]

477
00:24:33,767 --> 00:24:36,100
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE
STARTING, REVVING]

478
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,067
[GUNSHOTS]

479
00:24:37,067 --> 00:24:38,100
Surprise!

480
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:41,733
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

481
00:24:41,733 --> 00:24:43,367
Move the gold now! Hurry up!

482
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:45,533
[DJANGO SCREAMS]

483
00:24:45,533 --> 00:24:47,600
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

484
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:51,367
[GUNSHOTS IN THE BACKGROUND]

485
00:24:51,367 --> 00:24:57,233
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

486
00:24:57,233 --> 00:24:58,233
Keep going!

487
00:24:58,600 --> 00:24:59,733
- Come on!
- Let's go!

488
00:24:59,733 --> 00:25:02,733
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

489
00:25:02,767 --> 00:25:07,567
[GUNSHOTS IN DISTANCE]

490
00:25:07,567 --> 00:25:08,567
Boss, I'm here!

491
00:25:09,167 --> 00:25:10,700
Load it up!

492
00:25:11,767 --> 00:25:13,267
Come on, pick it up!

493
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:17,567
- You two, cover me!
- Sure, boss!

494
00:25:18,167 --> 00:25:19,500
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

495
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,433
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

496
00:25:24,300 --> 00:25:25,467
Where's Django?

497
00:25:25,467 --> 00:25:28,067
- He's still in there.
- Alright, move it now!

498
00:25:28,067 --> 00:25:29,067
Let's go!

499
00:25:29,433 --> 00:25:30,400
Hurry up!

500
00:25:30,933 --> 00:25:31,967
[GRUNTS]

501
00:25:31,967 --> 00:25:38,933
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

502
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:42,000
[POLICE SIREN BLARING]

503
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

504
00:25:44,467 --> 00:25:45,433
[GRUNTS]

505
00:25:45,933 --> 00:25:46,933
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

506
00:25:47,367 --> 00:25:48,367
[LAO] Let's go!

507
00:25:48,367 --> 00:25:51,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

508
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:55,167
[OVERLAPPING MURMURS]

509
00:25:55,167 --> 00:25:56,467
Hang on, everyone.

510
00:25:56,467 --> 00:26:00,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

511
00:26:00,133 --> 00:26:02,633
You need to understand,
at least somehow,

512
00:26:02,633 --> 00:26:05,000
that they have rights
to this land

513
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,367
since it's under their name.

514
00:26:06,367 --> 00:26:09,167
- [MAN 1] What?
- [WOMAN 1] How's that possible?

515
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:12,333
But that doesn't mean
you don't have any rights here.

516
00:26:12,333 --> 00:26:13,500
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

517
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:15,333
[MAN 2]
They'll drive us all out.

518
00:26:15,333 --> 00:26:19,400
[SAM] If the time ever comes
that you agree to a settlement,

519
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:21,900
you'll be given
a proper place to move to.

520
00:26:21,900 --> 00:26:26,900
With jobs, a school,
a hospital nearby...

521
00:26:26,900 --> 00:26:29,500
You'll have security
and stability.

522
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:31,167
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:26:31,167 --> 00:26:32,867
Maybe you can think about it.

524
00:26:32,867 --> 00:26:34,200
[INDISTINCT CROWD MURMURS]

525
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:36,500
- No way!
- We're not going anywhere!

526
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:43,467
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

527
00:26:44,033 --> 00:26:47,533
[DIDAY] Look, we can't leave
behind everything we've built.

528
00:26:47,533 --> 00:26:50,400
Yeah, we won't just walk away!

529
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:52,400
- This is our land!
- [WOMAN 2] We're staying!

530
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:53,933
[SAM] Hold on.

531
00:26:53,933 --> 00:26:56,267
I'm sorry,
that's not what I meant.

532
00:26:56,267 --> 00:26:58,033
You do have rights.

533
00:26:58,033 --> 00:26:59,400
We just have to be prepared

534
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:01,400
for whatever happens.

535
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:04,000
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

536
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,233
[ESTONG] Wait a minute, Gabo.

537
00:27:05,233 --> 00:27:07,400
Could the enemies
you fought the other night

538
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:09,367
and those fake NGO people
be working together?

539
00:27:09,367 --> 00:27:12,400
They'll really do anything
to force us out.

540
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:15,533
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

541
00:27:15,567 --> 00:27:16,700
[SAM] Exactly.

542
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:19,067
They'll do whatever it takes
to remove you.

543
00:27:19,067 --> 00:27:20,567
Even through violence.

544
00:27:20,567 --> 00:27:26,100
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

545
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,433
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

546
00:27:27,433 --> 00:27:29,433
[SAM]  Don't worry.

547
00:27:29,433 --> 00:27:32,400
<i> I'll do my best to help you.</i>

548
00:27:33,067 --> 00:27:36,400
<i>But Max showing up here
is a huge problem.</i>

549
00:27:36,933 --> 00:27:38,567
<i> They might track me down</i>

550
00:27:39,367 --> 00:27:42,567
<i>before I can find a way
to help you.</i>

551
00:27:45,067 --> 00:27:52,033
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

552
00:28:02,333 --> 00:28:05,300
<i>We found Sam's jacket
full of bullet holes.</i>

553
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:08,933
<i>I made her feel unworthy
of my affection.</i>

554
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:11,400
<i>This is divine punishment
for being a terrible father.</i>

555
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:14,167
<i> What made me fall for you?</i>

556
00:28:14,167 --> 00:28:16,733
<i>Obviously,
my looks top the list.</i>

557
00:28:16,733 --> 00:28:19,067
<i>Suppose Gloria's memories
come back.</i>

558
00:28:19,067 --> 00:28:20,233
<i> What happens to my son?</i>

559
00:28:20,233 --> 00:28:21,800
<i>He's already used
to having her around.</i>

560
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:24,333
<i>I guess I'm the luckiest man
in the world.</i>

561
00:28:24,367 --> 00:28:28,100
<i>I promise to look after you
and love you.</i>
